Aerie-Purpose: Keep crash reports on the device: no pending report is deleted at startup, only the oldest beyond 20 are, and nothing can turn on a crash upload or request one.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: components/crash/core/app/crashpad.cc (ApplyUploadConsent, RequestSingleCrashUploadImpl); chrome/browser/crash_upload_list/helium_crash_reporting.cc, BUILD.gn
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #262, on top of crash/0001 (no upload URL, mode always Disabled). Helium deletes every
pending report at startup in Disabled mode, so no dump ever reached the user. Now a dump stays
in <user data>/Crash Reports/pending until the user deletes it on the Crash reports page of
Settings (crash/0003), and at startup the oldest beyond 20 are pruned on a thread-pool task
(components/aerie_crash_reports). Uploads stay impossible at the lowest level too: the
database's upload switch is only ever set to off, whatever consent a caller passes, and a
request to upload one report (the chrome://crashes button, the crash dialog) does nothing, because
an explicit request would bypass that switch. docs/crash-reports.md has the whole account.

